    "solution": "Move to the edge of the western phase floor and hop into the low gap. Dash left through the inlet while airborne: this spends the dash and removes both the departure floor and the receiving bridge. The outlet turns your remaining motion upward past the down-arrow crystal. Let the rise end; only the falling contact restores the dash. Dash up-right to restore the bridge beneath you and reach its tally. The tally opens the gun feed, but the bridge now blocks the converted shot. Jump and dash onto the broad eastern bank to withdraw that bridge; wait safely for the receiver and door, then walk out.",
    "nearestExisting": "F47 uses a returned dash and a phase ceiling; F13 removes a useful surface to open a later optical route. This room specifically requires falling directional recovery after a spent portal approach, then gives the same receiving bridge an opposing role as a projectile obstruction. The former grounded phase-flip route completed without the crystal; the revised phase departure floor disappears before it can return a free dash.",
    "novelty": "The resource now has a physical reason to be missing: the low inlet gap requires an airborne dash, and a grounded preparation dash removes its own support. The falling crystal supplies the next action. After the bridge serves as a landing, the tally makes it an obstruction to the shot needed for the exit.",
